    fix(graph): reuse TagTemplate::default_for in TagIndex::build

    TagIndex::build's per-package loop built each package's default tag
    template by hand-formatting "{name}@{version}" and re-parsing it via
    TagTemplate::parse, instead of calling the already-established
    callisto_model::TagTemplate::default_for -- the single source of truth
    for this exact value that release.rs's tag-name construction already
    uses via unwrap_or_else(|| callisto_model::TagTemplate::default_for(&package.id)).

    The two implementations diverged: TagTemplate::parse additionally
    validates git-ref-name legality, so tags.rs could reject a package
    name release.rs's path would accept unchecked. Switching to
    default_for removes that extra validation from this call site
    intentionally, aligning tags.rs with release.rs's already-shipped
    behavior rather than adding new validation to default_for itself
    (a larger change affecting every caller). Documented in the
    changeset. Custom tag_template configs still go through
    TagTemplate::parse unchanged.

    Added a test asserting TagIndex::build's default template matches
    TagTemplate::default_for's output exactly; no existing test exercised
    the removed validate-and-reject behavior at this call site.

