Author: Gabe Castro <gabe@techworx.dev>
Date:   Wed Sep 9 07:40:50 2026 -0700

    fix(graph): guard against stale fixed-group members in cascade convergence

    solve_cascade's Fixed-group ("Track 1") convergence block was a structural
    copy of the Linked-group block directly above it, but never received the
    stale-member guard the Linked-group block got in 08814168. If a
    [[fixed-group]] in callisto.toml still named a package removed from the
    workspace, and a live sibling in that group received nonzero severity
    during cascade convergence, the Fixed-group loop unconditionally wrote
    the stale id into CascadeOutcome.severities/.targets for every id in
    g.package_members(), with no input.base.contains_key(id) check.

    That stale id then reached plan_version's
    pkg_map.get(id).copied().unwrap() (pkg_map is built only from live graph
    packages), panicking and crashing `callisto version` instead of degrading
    gracefully the way aggregate::union_fixed already does for the identical
    scenario.

    Mirror the Linked-group block's guard verbatim: filter
    g.package_members() into live_members via input.base.contains_key(id),
    push an UnknownPackage diagnostic (governed by ConfigKey::FIXED_GROUP)
    for each stale id, and iterate live_members (not the raw
    g.package_members()) in both the severity-raise loop and the
    target-insert loop.

    Adds a cascade.rs unit test exercising solve_cascade directly (confirms
    the stale id never enters severities/targets, and the diagnostic is
    emitted), plus a version.rs regression test that reproduces the actual
    pkg_map.get(id).copied().unwrap() panic on the pre-fix code path and
    confirms plan_version now completes cleanly with the diagnostic surfaced
    on VersionPlan.diagnostics.

    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED

