    refactor(graph,manifests): dedup OpenContext construction; open owner manifest once per platform group

    Add OpenContext::for_workspace_root as the single reusable constructor for
    the "check Cargo.toml exists, load workspace inheritance, detect npm
    workspace kind" sequence that walk.rs, Workspace::base_versions, apply.rs,
    and plan_version each reimplemented independently. Migrate all four call
    sites.

    plan_version's platform-target loop also re-opened a fixed group's owner
    manifest from disk once per platform sibling purely to check for a
    matching optional dependency, even though the owner's dependency list
    can't change across those iterations. Route that read through the
    workspace's existing read-only manifest_cache so it happens at most once
    per run regardless of platform-target count. A new regression test proves
    the fix by asserting open_call_count directly (and fails at 4 instead of 2
    opens when reverted).

