    fix(moon): classify native spawn failures by ErrorKind, not message text

    MoonCommandRunner::run's native path stringified a spawn io::Error
    before classifying it as NotFound vs Io, matching "not found"/"no such
    file" substrings in the lowercased Display text. That heuristic is a
    locale/wording-dependent proxy for something the stdlib already
    type-checks: ErrorKind::NotFound. A non-English locale or a future
    libc wording change could silently misclassify an ENOENT-class error
    as CommandError::Io, breaking the "tool isn't installed" UX several
    call sites branch on CommandError::NotFound for.

