Author: Gabe Castro <gabe@techworx.dev>
Date:   Wed Sep 9 09:43:45 2026 -0700

    perf(graph,moon): memoize IdentityResolver::resolve to fix redundant identity resolution

    IdentityResolver::resolve did a fresh fs::read_to_string + full manifest
    parse on every call with zero memoization. MoonProjectLocator::declared_edges
    independently re-resolved every project's identity a second time even though
    projects() (called earlier in the same flow) already resolved it once, and
    worse, re-resolved a dependency edge's target once per edge instead of once
    per unique target project -- a widely-depended-on package (e.g. a shared
    crate with 30 internal dependents) had its manifest read and parsed 30+
    times in a single Workspace::load.

    IdentityResolver now memoizes resolve()'s result by (path, ecosystem) behind
    a Mutex (ProjectLocator requires Send + Sync) for the resolver's whole
    lifetime. Since MoonProjectLocator holds one IdentityResolver across both
    projects() and declared_edges(), a given manifest is now read and parsed at
    most once per run -- no structural change needed in declared_edges itself.

    Adds a process-global identity_read_count/reset_identity_read_count test
    counter (mirroring callisto_manifests::open_call_count) and three regression
    tests: two inline memoization unit tests in identity.rs (one proving a
    second resolve() call survives the manifest file being deleted, one proving
    distinct (path, ecosystem) keys don't collide), plus two #[serial] count
    tests -- one driving IdentityResolver directly (30 calls, 1 read), one
    driving the real MoonProjectLocator flow with 5 dependents naming one
    shared "utils" package (6 manifests read via projects(), still 6 after
    declared_edges() resolves the 5 edges onto it, not 11).

