    fix(graph,model): filter stale members in fixed-group target, fix ReleaseOperationId/ArtifactSlotId Ord/Eq consistency

    Track 1 (fixed-group convergence) passed the raw, unfiltered GroupDef
    into fixed_group_target, so a group member removed from the workspace
    but still declared in callisto.toml -- if it carried a leftover release
    tag -- could be picked as the alignment base and silently fall back to
    1.0.0 when its (missing) base version lookup failed, corrupting the
    target for every live sibling. fixed_group_target now takes an
    already-filtered live_members slice, mirroring the guard the
    Linked-group block already applies.

    Separately, ReleaseOperationId's and ArtifactSlotId's hand-written Ord
    impls keyed their Version field on render() alone, dropping grammar.
    The same literal string parses under more than one grammar ("1.2.3" is
    valid SemVer and PEP 440), so two Eq-distinct values could compare
    Ordering::Equal, violating the BTreeSet/BTreeMap invariant. Both now
    key on (grammar, raw) via a shared version_ord_key helper.

